      "previewImage": "previews/minimax-h3-heptagram-turbo-t2v.jpg",
      "description": "eatyet's Heptagram Turbo v1.0 (21.0 GB) on the plain official graph at the author's settings: res_multistep / simple, 8 steps, sigma shift 12 video / 3 audio. His stated ranges are 4 to 8 steps and shift 6 to 16; the Steps control covers 4 to 8. The speed LoRAs are part of the checkpoint, so there is no LoRA node and no second file.\n\nThis one has a look. The author says it works well for game, anime and 3D styles. In a one-seed comparison against eight other H3 checkpoints (2026-10-09, RTX 4070 Ti 12 GB, 864x480, 15 s, engine v0.38.0) on a prompt that asked for needle-felt stop-motion and excluded 3D CGI, it gave a smooth 3D-animated character with bright glints on the glass on two of three prompt versions. A structured three-shot brief pulled it back to a felt look and cut at the scripted 5 and 10 second marks. Choose it for stylised 3D animation, not for handmade or photographic texture. One seed and one scene, so treat this as a first impression.\n\nThe author notes that the audio in this version has some flaws; we did not judge the audio by ear.\n\nAbout 5 1/2 minutes per 15-second clip at 480p. Free system RAM matters more than VRAM; keep 16 GB+ free.\n\nVerified in SimpliGen 1.71.1 / engine v0.38.0 on a 12 GB RTX 4070 Ti: 15 s at 864x480, 8 steps, 338 s through the app, and the output matched the engine test frame for frame (same seed).",
